Derk Norton (dnorton@advtech.uswest.com) wrote:
: Can multiple threads within a DCE *client* share a fully bound binding
: handle without using a mutex for the handle?  If so, are there any
: other precautions I should take when doing so?

I believe that you can use a single binding handle to concurrently
make calls from multiple threads.  However, you _are_ likely to get
into problems concurrently doing other "non-call" operations on the
shared binding handle; e.g., I wouldn't advise doing something like
rpc_binding_reset() from one thread while doing the same (_or_ making
a remote call) on the same binding handle from another thread.

Also, as best I can recall, we did go to some effort to make the
concurrent call case work even when the binding handle isn't "fully
bound" to a server (although one call may stall until the other call
has successfully resolved to a server).
