Derk Norton <dnorton@advtech.uswest.com> wrote:
>Hello,
>Can multiple threads within a DCE *client* share a fully bound binding
>handle without using a mutex for the handle?  If so, are there any
>other precautions I should take when doing so?

I've tried it and it works -- however, that's only when using the binding
handle to make RPCs. If you want to rebind or call a function in the
DCE API that takes a binding handle, it'd be best to play it safe and
put a mutex on the handle. If you lock the handle whenever you call a
DCE API function and check if it's locked before every RPC, you should
be fine.

