	This is not true. In OSF/1 and other thread oriented OS's 
	thread is minimum unit of execution - each thread can be
	scheduled individually and can execute parallel in different
	processor. So in fact thread based solution can reach much higher
	level of parallelism as it can use both processes and threads to
	increase the level of concurrent execution.

	There are different implementations in other operating systems 
