Derk,

Regarding your question:

> Can multiple threads within a DCE *client* share a fully bound binding
> handle without using a mutex for the handle?  If so, are there any
> other precautions I should take when doing so?
> Thanks in advance,
> Derk
> 

Though it is, in general, possible to do, expecially if you follow the
guidelines mentioned in the two previous responses, I would be more
inclined to give each thread its own binding handle.  Don't forget that
rpc_binding_copy() will dup a binding handle.  You can use thread
specific storage, pthread_cleaup_push(), and pthread_cleaup_pop() to
manage the memory for the per thread binding handles.  This would be
useful in case you don't know how many threads (and therefore how many
handles) you'll be using.  I started out trying to share binding handles
and quickly realized that I would have many fewer headaches using copies.

