There is no bug here. If you do not restrict the use of protocol
sequences, by calling rpc_server_use_protseq instead of
rpc_server_use_all_protseqs, then the RPC runtime will create a
binding for each transport that it supports. In your case, one for DG
(ncadg_ip_udp) and one for CN (ncacn_ip_tcp).

This is explained quite well in the DCE Application Development Guide.

Jonathan

