Hopefully someone will give you a better answer, but as I usderstand
it ANDF is Application Neutral Distribution Format.

The idea is that you compile to an ANDF intermediate code, and
on the target architecture run an installer which produces the
appropriate binary.

If the installer comes with your box, you could then buy "srink wrapped"
software at "Egghead" and install it on whatever architecture
you happened to be running.

You should be able to get info from OSF.


